      <data key="d2">cb-0304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR II&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War II was a global conflict that lasted from 1939 to 1945, involving most of the world's nations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NON-JEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Non-Jews refer to individuals who are not of Jewish descent, specifically highlighting the 26,000 non-Jews recognized as Righteous Among the Nations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;26,000 NON-JEWS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUMBER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"26,000 non-Jews have been recognized as Righteous Among the Nations since the award's inception in 1963."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;123 AMERICAN RECIPIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUMBER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"123 American recipients have been recognized as Righteous Among the Nations, including Heidi Kitrosser."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNSUNG HEROES OF THE HOLOCAUST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unsung heroes of the Holocaust are individuals whose brave actions during the Holocaust were not widely known until recent research and testimonies."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0304</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KITROSSER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
